{% doc %}
  Renders supplemental buying guidance for priority collection landing pages.

  @param {collection} collection - The active collection.
{% enddoc %}

{% assign collection_handle = collection.handle | downcase %}
{% assign priority_collection_handles = 'bondage,chastity,lingerie,roleplay,men,women,couples,bdsm' | split: ',' %}
{% capture content %}
  {% case collection_handle %}
    {% when 'bondage' or 'bdsm' %}
      <h2>Bondage gear: choose for comfort, communication and control</h2>
      <p>Bondage can be as simple as a soft cuff or as considered as a multi-piece restraint set. Start by deciding what kind of sensation and movement you want: light positioning, adjustable wrist or ankle restraint, decorative harness styling, or a more structured setup. Read every product page before ordering so you can compare closure type, adjustability, materials, dimensions and the pieces included.</p>
      <p>For a first purchase, prioritise adjustable designs and a fit that can be checked easily. Avoid using any restraint that causes pain, numbness, tingling, colour changes or restricted breathing. Keep a quick-release option or safety shears available when appropriate, agree on boundaries and a safeword before play, and never leave a restrained person unattended. Cleaning and storage guidance can differ by material, so follow the care instructions supplied with the item.</p>
      <p>Explore related <a href="/collections/chastity">chastity accessories</a>, <a href="/collections/roleplay">roleplay styles</a> and the <a href="/pages/knowledge-base">Knowledge Base</a> for sizing, care and safety guidance. Check the individual listing for stock, shipping and return eligibility before purchase.</p>
      <p>Build confidence gradually. Read product dimensions before choosing cuffs, collars or rope, and make sure every participant can communicate clearly throughout the experience. A product’s appearance does not tell you whether it is adjustable, washable or suitable for your intended use, so treat the listing and care instructions as the source of truth. If a detail is missing, contact support before ordering. Choosing fewer, well-understood pieces is usually more useful than adding items without a clear purpose.</p>
    {% when 'chastity' %}
      <h2>Chastity accessories: fit and care come first</h2>
      <p>Choosing a chastity accessory starts with fit, not appearance. Compare the measurements shown on each product page with your own needs, including ring size, internal dimensions, adjustment method and the type of closure. A comfortable, secure fit should never create pain, numbness, rubbing, swelling or changes in circulation. If you are new to the category, choose a style that is easy to remove and keep early sessions short while you learn what works for you.</p>
      <p>Read the listed material and care instructions before use. Different finishes and components may need different cleaning methods, and a product should be inspected before every session for sharp edges, damage or parts that do not operate smoothly. Good communication, clear boundaries and a readily available way to remove the item are essential. Never force a fit or continue if there is discomfort.</p>
      <p>For a complete setup, browse <a href="/collections/bondage">bondage and restraint gear</a> or <a href="/collections/couples">couples’ accessories</a>. The <a href="/pages/knowledge-base">Knowledge Base</a> includes practical care and sizing resources. Confirm variant availability, delivery timing and return conditions on the product page before ordering.</p>
      <p>Plan for comfort before duration. Begin with a short fitting check in a private, relaxed setting and make sure removal is straightforward before extending wear. Hydration, movement, temperature and individual anatomy can all affect comfort, so do not rely on another person’s sizing experience. Keep the product clean and dry between uses, and replace it if a component becomes damaged or difficult to operate. Where a listing provides fitting guidance, follow it in preference to general online advice.</p>
    {% when 'lingerie' %}
      <h2>Lingerie: compare fit, fabric and styling details</h2>
      <p>Lingerie should feel as considered as it looks. Use the size chart and garment measurements on each listing rather than relying only on a usual clothing size, especially for fitted, stretch, mesh or strappy designs. Check the product photographs, closure type, adjustable straps and included pieces so you understand how the style is intended to fit. If you are choosing a gift, a flexible fit or adjustable option can make selection easier.</p>
      <p>Fabric composition and care instructions matter. Review the product description for the material, finish and washing guidance, then follow the manufacturer’s care recommendations to help preserve shape and colour. Avoid making assumptions about stretch, opacity or support when they are not stated on the listing. For intimate apparel, review the store’s current hygiene and return conditions before purchase, as eligibility can vary by product and local requirements.</p>
      <p>Pair lingerie with <a href="/collections/roleplay">roleplay styles</a>, browse <a href="/collections/women">women’s collections</a> or see the <a href="/pages/knowledge-base">Knowledge Base</a> for care information. Check the selected colour, size, availability and delivery details before adding an item to your cart.</p>
      <p>To make comparison easier, note the information that affects wear: whether a fabric is described as stretch or structured, whether straps or closures adjust, and whether multiple pieces are included. Measure at the points named in the size guide and leave room for personal comfort. Keep new garments in their original condition until you are sure they are right for you, subject to the published return policy. When in doubt between two sizes, use the product’s own chart and contact support with a non-sensitive sizing question.</p>
    {% when 'roleplay' %}
      <h2>Roleplay styles: choose a look that supports the experience</h2>
      <p>Roleplay is personal, so begin with a style, theme or accessory that feels comfortable for everyone involved. Costumes, masks, harnesses and themed pieces can set a mood without requiring a complex setup. Use the product pages to compare sizing, adjustability, materials and what is included. Selecting an item that is easy to wear, remove and care for can make a new experience feel more relaxed.</p>
      <p>Clear conversation is the foundation of any roleplay experience. Agree on the scenario, boundaries, a pause signal and aftercare before you begin. If an item adds restraint, pressure or reduced visibility, take additional care with fit, circulation and communication. Do not use a costume or accessory in a way it was not designed for, and stop immediately if it causes discomfort, pain or distress.</p>
      <p>Find complementary <a href="/collections/lingerie">lingerie</a>, <a href="/collections/bondage">bondage gear</a> and <a href="/collections/couples">couples’ accessories</a>. For practical guidance on care, consent and selecting your first item, visit the <a href="/pages/knowledge-base">Knowledge Base</a> before you shop.</p>
      <p>Set expectations before buying an item for a shared scenario. Discuss what each person enjoys, what is off limits and how you will pause or stop if the experience changes. Choose products that match the level of control and sensation you both want, and do not treat a costume or prop as a substitute for communication. After use, check in with one another, clean products as directed and store them safely. Small, well-planned additions often create a better experience than a complicated setup.</p>
    {% when 'men' %}
      <h2>Men’s intimate accessories: select with clear product details</h2>
      <p>Browse men’s intimate accessories by the experience, fit and features that matter most to you. Product pages should help you compare dimensions, materials, adjustment options, compatible accessories and care requirements before ordering. When a product comes in more than one size, colour or configuration, select the exact variant and review its availability before adding it to your cart.</p>
      <p>Comfort and safe use should guide every choice. Follow the manufacturer’s instructions, inspect an item before use and stop if it causes pain, numbness, irritation or injury. Clean and store each item according to its material-specific care guidance. For products used with lubricants, check the listing and lubricant instructions for compatibility rather than assuming that every combination is suitable.</p>
      <p>You can also explore <a href="/collections/chastity">chastity accessories</a>, <a href="/collections/bondage">bondage gear</a> and <a href="/collections/couples">couples’ collections</a>. Visit the <a href="/pages/knowledge-base">Knowledge Base</a> for sizing, cleaning and safety resources, then review shipping and returns information before purchase.</p>
      <p>Make a considered comparison before selecting an item. Look beyond the title and price to the specifications, product images, variant selection and maintenance instructions. A listing that does not state a dimension, material or feature should not be interpreted as a guarantee. Choose equipment that you understand how to use and can remove safely. If you are purchasing an accessory with moving parts, locks or adjustable pieces, check that it is complete and functioning as described when it arrives before first use.</p>
    {% when 'women' %}
      <h2>Women’s intimate accessories: compare fit, features and care</h2>
      <p>Women’s intimate accessories range from lingerie and sensory toys to roleplay pieces and personal-care essentials. Start with the purpose, shape, size and features you prefer, then use each product page to compare the stated materials, dimensions, included components and care instructions. Selecting a product with clear information makes it easier to choose a suitable option for your preferences and experience level.</p>
      <p>Always follow the manufacturer’s guidance for cleaning, storage and intended use. Inspect products before use, do not share items unless they can be cleaned appropriately, and stop if anything causes irritation, pain, numbness or injury. If you use lubricant, check the product and lubricant instructions for compatibility. For lingerie, use the size chart and garment details rather than assuming a standard fit.</p>
      <p>Browse <a href="/collections/lingerie">lingerie</a>, <a href="/collections/roleplay">roleplay styles</a> and <a href="/collections/couples">couples’ accessories</a>. The <a href="/pages/knowledge-base">Knowledge Base</a> offers guidance on sizing, materials and care. Confirm your chosen variant, delivery details and return eligibility on the listing before ordering.</p>
      <p>Give yourself time to compare options rather than choosing from images alone. Product specifications, size guidance and care details are more reliable indicators of suitability than a broad category label. Start with a simple design if you are trying a new type of item, and avoid using any product beyond its stated purpose. Keep packaging and documentation until you have reviewed the condition and the store’s return rules. If you need help finding an item with a specific feature, ask support before placing an order.</p>
    {% when 'couples' %}
      <h2>Couples’ accessories: shop together and communicate clearly</h2>
      <p>Couples’ accessories can support shared exploration, whether you are choosing a simple gift, a sensory item, lingerie or a more structured roleplay setup. The best starting point is a conversation about interests, boundaries, comfort and what each person would like to try. Then compare product details together, including materials, dimensions, adjustment options, included parts and care requirements.</p>
      <p>Choose products that are suited to your experience level and are easy to use as intended. For anything involving restraint, pressure, reduced visibility or intense sensation, agree on a safeword or pause signal, keep communication open and stop immediately if either person is uncomfortable. Follow cleaning and storage instructions, inspect items before use and avoid assumptions about lubricant compatibility or material safety when the listing does not provide that information.</p>
      <p>Continue with <a href="/collections/bondage">bondage gear</a>, <a href="/collections/roleplay">roleplay styles</a> or <a href="/collections/lingerie">lingerie</a>. The <a href="/pages/knowledge-base">Knowledge Base</a> has practical resources on communication, sizing and care. Review delivery, privacy and return details before completing your order.</p>
      <p>Shopping together can make selection clearer and more enjoyable. Compare the stated specifications side by side, agree on a budget and decide what information you need before checkout. If either person is unsure, choose a lower-intensity option or wait until you have more information. Respect a change of mind at any point. Once an item arrives, inspect it, read the care guidance and talk through how it will be used before trying it. Good planning supports a more relaxed shared experience.</p>
  {% endcase %}
  {% if priority_collection_handles contains collection_handle %}
    <p>Before checkout, take a final moment to review the exact variant in your cart, the stated product specifications and the current policy pages. Product availability, delivery estimates and return eligibility can change, so the information shown at purchase is the information to rely on. Use the collection as a starting point, then make your final decision from the individual product listing. For personal support, contact the store with a clear question before ordering rather than making assumptions about features or fit.</p>
  {% endif %}
{% endcapture %}

{% if content != blank %}
  <section class="collection-seo-content" aria-label="Collection buying guide">
    <div class="collection-seo-content__inner rte">{{ content }}</div>
  </section>
{% endif %}

